{
  "about": "Colour pairs that must stay readable, checked by pnpm check in every look and both themes. fg and bg are variable names without the dashes, resolved the way css/*.css resolves them. min is the WCAG contrast ratio: 4.5 for text, 3 for large text (24px, or 18.5px bold) and for parts of the UI that carry meaning, like focus rings and the edges of controls. fg can be a list when a mark is drawn in more than one colour, like Discothèque's two-band focus ring: the pair passes when any of them reads on bg. looks limits a pair to one look. docs/foundations.md shows these tables; pnpm build writes them.",
